                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>This course comprehensively expounds the management concepts and methods of hospital infection control from all aspects, including the concept of standard precautions such as hand hygiene, personal protection, disinfection and isolation techniques, and occupational exposure; evidence-based prevention and control measures for key site infections like catheter-associated bloodstream infections, ventilator-associated pneumonia, and surgical site infections; diagnosis and treatment of infectious diseases involving microbiological specimen collection and rational use of antimicrobial drugs; as well as prevention and control of communicable diseases including respiratory infectious diseases and waterborne infectious diseases.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
